Bug fix: add pill surface to world-space collision — pillChordDist() for hemispherical caps.

This commit modifies 2 files (+141/-2 lines), spanning 1 game server, 1 Markdown docs.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
Audit found pill was missing from usesWorldDist in GameRoom.ts. Near hemispherical
caps, UV U-coordinate compresses (same as capsule/sphere poles), causing UV distance
to underestimate world distance by up to 3×. Enemies near caps could pass through.

Added pillChordDist() with exact 3D chord distance for pill geometry (cylinder body +
hemispherical caps). Constants match PillSurface.ts (radius=4, height=16).

Worker OOM-killed mid-audit. Remaining surfaces (mobius, cylinder, cube, plane, klein)
still use UV fallback — may need future audit.

